- Story & Context: When an unexpected squall threatened to tear the tent away during the 2017 totality over Makanda, Illinois, Deacon Vance refused to pause, spitting sixteen-bar cycles through a dented copper megaphone while the smell of ozone and damp canvas choked the room. A snapped guy-wire lashed into the rhythm section's trunk-drum, sparking an impromptu mechanical groove that the crowd mistook for carnival magic. The performance cemented the Syndicate's rule of never repeating a chorus, punctuated only by Vance snarling, "Cut the stalk to the quick, watch the black wheel stick."
