Track 2: Sister Hallowell’s Coldframe
- Story & Context: Penned inside an unheated glass greenhouse outside Carbondale, this confession recounts the night herbalist Sister Hallowell cracked the fairground padlock to reclaim heritage tomato seeds confiscated by county inspectors. With sweat freezing on the glass panes and flashlights sweeping the perimeter, Vance documented her testimony over a single, cyclical two-chord Mellotron string patch that refused to resolve. Her defiant testimony became the track's spine when she muttered into the vocal mic, "I buried every dime in the loam before the sun died."
