Track 3: Did the Spore Catch When the Sky Shut?
- Story & Context: Legend surrounds the final performance at Devil's Backbone Ridge, where local deputies raided the eclipse midway only to find thirty silent spectators standing in a circle around an unattended reel-to-reel deck still spinning against a deadened banjo loop. The syndicate had vanished down the ravine on foot, leaving behind only the sulfurous stench of extinguished flares and an iron anchor driven into a ring of black nightshade. As the tape ran out of leader, Vance’s voice lingered from the horn speaker, asking, "No harvest comes back when the crown goes black."
